            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Roger Gili Coscojuela",
                        "email": "roger.gili-coscojuela@sipearl.com",
                        "username": "Wewannado"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the patch, it really helps out new openbmc members. However, I have some concerns that I would like you to address."
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 233,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Roger Gili Coscojuela",
                        "email": "roger.gili-coscojuela@sipearl.com",
                        "username": "Wewannado"
                    },
                    "message": "It would be better to actually explain how to reuse this folders.\n\nBy default, bitbake generates and mantain the sstate cache and downloads folder by itself, no need to configure anything.\n\nThe only reason I see to actually set up this folders in the local.conf is if you share a common folder between team members, and even then, I'm not sure if bitbake will complain about having them in a nfs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 233,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It's also useful when you want to separately build multiple machines.  I've long configured an external sstate and downloads folder because I build many different platforms plus 2 different layer sets (open source + meta-specific layers)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 233,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "Should I include details about SSTATE_MIRRORS, or would that be too much information here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 233,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's do the SSTATE_MIRRORS as a separate cjommit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 239,
                    "reviewer": {
