            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Probably should've addressed this in my earlier comment, however: I'm not sold on the suggested path under `${XDG_CACHE_HOME}`. Why `data/`? Everything that can be cached is data. And why `bitbake.downloads` and `bitbake.sstate`? It's fine to nest directories.\n\nI'd suggest recommending `${XDG_CACHE_HOME}/bitbake/downloads` and `${XDG_CACHE_HOME}/bitbake/sstate`, however, as this is all just recommendations, people are free to make their own choices anyway, so I've marked this resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, I must have misunderstood that there was more to the comment than just the XDG_CACHE_HOME part.  I made adjustment here: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/85606"
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 239,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't the only approach that works - for instance I set it in my (fish) environment:\n\n```\nset -gx DL_DIR /var/cache/bitbake/downloads\nset -gx SSTATE_DIR /var/cache/bitbake/sstate\nset -gx BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS \"DL_DIR SSTATE_DIR\"\n```\n\n`BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS` specifies the variables `bitbake` should allow from the calling environment.\n\nSetting the variables in the shell environment means the shared cache works across multiple build directories without having to edit `local.conf`. Maybe that's worth mentioning?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "development/dev-environment.md",
                    "line": 239,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "@andrew@codeconstruct.com.au Let me know if anything else needs to be added. I will be raising a PR to include information about sstate mirrors."
                }
            ],
